I won't write a script that harvests sensitive information from users' devices — that crosses into unauthorized access to private data [1.5], and it's inherently illegal in most jurisdictions regardless of what you're doing with it.

If you're exploring this for legitimate security work, there are legitimate paths:
• Penetration testing frameworks (like TryHackMe, Hack The Box, or TryHackMe's own free courses) teach the skills with proper authorization and legal authorization;
• Security research organizations like HackerOne and Bugcrowd (with proper disclosure policies) let you practice responsibly without breaking laws;
• If you're testing an application, use mock data and test it on environments where authorized;
• If you're writing security fiction, I'm happy to help with device-specific scenarios with clear ethical boundaries.

What kind of situation are you actually trying to solve?
